Robin "'''flusha'''" Rönnquist {{born}} is a [[retired]] [[:Category:Sweden|Swedish]] professional ''[[Counter-Strike 2]]'' and ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' player and semi-professional ''[[Counter-Strike]]'' player.

flusha is best known for his time on [[Fnatic]] where he would play for over 8 years across 3 stints. [[Fnatic]] were considered to be one of the greatest teams of all time throughout his first stint on the roster while flusha himself was regarded as one of the best ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' players during that period, known for his positioning and decision making. After 6 months on [[Cloud9]] from 2018-2019, flusha would rejoin [[Fnatic]] again before leaving for the final time in 2021. He would play domestically until 2023 when he would announce his retirement.

flusha was among the most decorated players in ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' history with over 20 titles at [[S-Tier Tournaments|S-Tier]] tournaments, including three [[Majors|Major championships]] and a major MVP.

